  m_text: <b>The Deccan Plateau </b>covers a large part of southern India and is
    bordered by the Western and Eastern Ghats. It is made of ancient volcanic rocks
    and has black soil that is very good for growing cotton. Many important rivers
    like the Godavari, Krishna, and Kaveri flow through this plateau.
